 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "Governments all over Europe just shut down a bunch of their own websites on PURPOSE, because of this bug where hackers could take over a site without a password.",
   "s": 0.19,
   "e": 8.18,
   "words": [
    0,
    28
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "It's in PHP\u2026 the language everyone loves, and about seven out of ten websites run on it.",
   "s": 8.605,
   "e": 13.945,
   "words": [
    29,
    45
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "This bug was in there for like fourteen years before researchers using AI figured out how bad it was.",
   "s": 14.395,
   "e": 19.565,
   "words": [
    46,
    64
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "They gave the PHP people a heads-up, but word got out before the fix was ready, and hackers were ALREADY trying to use it.",
   "s": 19.98,
   "e": 26.325,
   "words": [
    65,
    88
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Cloudflare says that once it was announced, they saw tens of thousands of hacking attempts in forty-five minutes, and millions within a day.",
   "s": 26.79,
   "e": 34.25,
   "words": [
    89,
    111
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "But even with the fix out, somebody STILL has to install it on every single server.",
   "s": 34.715,
   "e": 39.35,
   "words": [
    112,
    127
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Plus something like HALF of PHP sites run versions so old they're not officially supported anymore.",
   "s": 39.705,
   "e": 45.385,
   "words": [
    128,
    143
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Even the FBI said if you can't update yet, just turn it off, which is basically tech support's answer to everything.",
   "s": 45.85,
   "e": 51.895,
   "words": [
    144,
    164
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "And some of those governments did it before there was even a fix.",
   "s": 52.43,
   "e": 55.235,
   "words": [
    165,
    177
   ]
  }
 ],
